## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- [Node.js](https://nodejs.org/) v18+
- [MongoDB](https://www.mongodb.com/) (local or Atlas)
- [Cloudinary Account](https://cloudinary.com/) (free tier works)
- [Clerk Account](https://clerk.dev/) (for OAuth setup)
- [Google Gemini API Key](https://makersuite.google.com/app/apikey)
- [Git](https://git-scm.com/)

---

### 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone https://github.com/shahbaz00000/ai-saas.git
cd ai-saas
```

---

### 2. Backend Setup

```bash
cd server
npm install
```

Create a `.env` file inside `/server`:

```env
# Server
PORT=5000

# MongoDB
MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_connection_string

# Google Gemini AI
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key

# Cloudinary
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME=your_cloud_name
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY=your_cloudinary_api_key
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET=your_cloudinary_api_secret

# Clerk Auth
CLERK_SECRET_KEY=your_clerk_secret_key
CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your_clerk_publishable_key
```

Start the backend:

```bash
npm run dev
```

> Server runs on `http://localhost:5000`

---

### 3. Frontend Setup

```bash
cd client
npm install
```

Create a `.env` file inside `/client`:

```env
REACT_APP_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your_clerk_publishable_key
REACT_APP_API_URL=http://localhost:5000
```

Start the frontend:

```bash
npm start
```

> React app runs on `http://localhost:3000`

---

## 🔐 API Endpoints

### Content Routes — `/api/content`

| Method | Endpoint | Description | Access |
|--------|----------|-------------|--------|
| `POST` | `/article` | Generate a full article | Private 🔒 |
| `POST` | `/blog-titles` | Generate blog title suggestions | Private 🔒 |
| `POST` | `/image` | Generate an AI image from prompt | Private 🔒 |

### Image Routes — `/api/image`

| Method | Endpoint | Description | Access |
|--------|----------|-------------|--------|
| `POST` | `/remove-background` | Remove image background (Cloudinary) | Private 🔒 |
| `POST` | `/remove-object` | Remove object from image (Cloudinary) | Private 🔒 |

### Resume Routes — `/api/resume`

| Method | Endpoint | Description | Access |
|--------|----------|-------------|--------|
| `POST` | `/analyze` | Upload & analyze resume with AI | Private 🔒 |
| `GET` | `/history` | Get past resume analyses | Private 🔒 |

---

## 🔐 Clerk OAuth Setup

1. Create a free account at [clerk.dev](https://clerk.dev)
2. Create a new application
3. Enable **Google** and/or **GitHub** as social providers
4. Copy your **Publishable Key** and **Secret Key** into `.env`
5. Set your allowed redirect URLs:
   - Development: `http://localhost:3000`
   - Production: `https://your-deployed-domain.com`

```
User clicks "Sign in with Google"
        ↓
   Clerk handles OAuth flow
        ↓
   JWT issued by Clerk
        ↓
   Backend verifies token via Clerk middleware
        ↓
   User session established ✅
```

